    "turn_text": "It was opposed by 198 Democrats. That's not a good look. Tony Katz, 93 W.I.B.C. Good morning. Congressman Jim Banks got to be with us in just a few minutes to discuss it. Meanwhile, Representative Acasio-Cortez in a full fit of tantrum has brought the articles of impeachment against justices a Samuel Lido and Clarence Thomas. And when asked why on what grounds she said because they gave me the sads. She also continued by saying, I hate old white men. And someone reminded her that Clarence Thomas was black. And she said, no, that was that was the official quote from representative Acasio Cortez. Nothing's coming of this. It's not going to get voted for. It's not going anywhere. It was a posturing move. What else can one do when your bestie Jamal Bowman loses a primary? because you don't like the other Democrat because he's not Hamas liking enough. All right, I don't know if that's an actual quote, but that's I that's the generalized feel again from Acasio-Cortez. The resolution states that Clarence Thomas engaged in high crimes and misdemeanors by failing to report travel accommodations and tuition for his grand nephew provided by a donor, as well as free rent and home improvements related to a 2014 real estate transaction between the justice and a man by the name of Harlan Crow, who's a donor to Republicans. When George Soros donates, everything is fine. And if you mention him, you're an anti-Semite. Also, you're not an anti-Semite when you mention George Soros. I will talk about George Soros anytime I choose. If you'd like to call me an anti-Semite, please check with my rabbi and get back to me. It's fine. We're going to be just fine people. It's laughable. Did you hear that Huma Abadine? Do you remember Huma Abadine? She was the one who was married to Anthony Wiener. She was the one who was, you know, Inka Hoots with Hillary Clinton, Vice Chair of the Campaign for President, Deputy Chief of Staff, which she was Secretary of State. Huma Abidine is