    "turn_text": "talking to congressman jim banks of the indiana third district republican candidate for senate in the state uh... of of indiana uh... we talk about the the border and certainly it's been a kind of secondary subject as of late and i'll get into why uh... in in a minute we have seen though that the president had long said that he doesn't have the power. You need to give him the power. You need to give him this vote. You had to vote for the bipartisan bill put forth by people like Senator Sinema and Senator James Langford, Republican of Oklahoma, and then that did not go through. And the next thing you know, You have him saying, well, I'll do these things on my own as if he always had the power to begin with. So now that it's been a few weeks past that, are you seeing or hearing from people on border patrol who follow these things? We're getting a better result. We had heard last week that crossings were down. Does it continue to trend in that direction or was that a temporary thing?",
